Falsifies `kernel::virtio::tests::a_device_write_to_the_read_only_shadow_is_refused`.

Architecture: x86_64
Environment: NIFE_IOMMU=amd

The defect: `virtio_regions` grants the shadow page writable again, which is what every domain
carried before provisional milestone 767 (AMD-Vi hardening before the first AMD boot). The device
can then rewrite the descriptor table and available ring the kernel validated, and the test's
used ring, pointed into that page, takes the device's writes.

Expected to fail: the test's `assert_eq!(flags, 0xffff, ...)`. QEMU's virtio-blk sets and then
clears `VRING_USED_F_NO_NOTIFY` when kicked, so the canary reads `0xfffe`. The record is the AMD-Vi
machine's because that is this milestone's unit, but the claim is portable and so is the patch:
measured on patagonia 2026-10-05 (UTC), QEMU 11.1.1, it fails the same way with
`NIFE_IOMMU=amd`, on the default VT-d machine and on aarch64's SMMUv3.

diff --git a/kernel/src/iommu.rs b/kernel/src/iommu.rs
index 5830c861d..d767beef7 100644
--- a/kernel/src/iommu.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/iommu.rs
@@ -241,7 +241,7 @@ pub fn virtio_regions(
         DmaRegion {
             base: shadow_base,
             size: page_frames::FRAME_SIZE,
-            writable: false,
+            writable: true,
         },
     ]
 }
